  "rulebook_source": "rulebook_id: agent-guard\nversion: 1.0.0\nadopted_at: \"2026-08-05T00:00:00Z\"\ndescription: Gate an AI agent's tool calls and shell commands.\ntrack: [workspace]\nevidence:\n  - {id: approvals, source: file, ref: .vfy/approvals.json, max_age_seconds: 86400, required: false}\nrules:\n  - id: no-destructive-shell\n    when: 'candidate.action.argv[0] in [\"rm\",\"mkfs\",\"dd\",\"shutdown\"] or matches(candidate.action.summary, \"*rm -rf*\")'\n    outcome: BLOCK\n    reason: Destructive shell commands are never allowed.\n  - id: write-inside-workspace\n    when: 'candidate.kind == \"tool_call\" and candidate.action.tool == \"write_file\" and matches(candidate.action.params.path, \"./workspace/*\")'\n    outcome: ALLOW\n    reason: Writes inside the declared workspace are allowed.\n  - id: outbound-email-needs-approval\n    when: 'candidate.action.tool == \"send_email\" and not present(approvals)'\n    outcome: HOLD\n    reason: External email requires a recorded human approval.\n  - id: undeclared-network\n    when: 'candidate.kind == \"http_request\" and not matches(candidate.action.targets[0], \"https://api.internal.example/*\")'\n    outcome: BLOCK\n    reason: Only declared network destinations are allowed.\ndefault_outcome: HOLD\nauthorization: {ttl_seconds: 120, single_use: true}\n",
